'''Helmet Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Catnip Challenges]] during the [[Anniversary/13th Year|13th Anniversary]]. It was added in [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]] for [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] and in [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]] for [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 833
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Helmet Cat
|name2 = Yellow Nyanko Ranger
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Yellow Nyanko Ranger''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat has a unique role as an anti-[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] tank that can even be used in {{4c}} restriction stages. The lack of proper tanks available for Dark enemies makes their role valuable regardless of their performance; that said, while effective on paper, their recharge time and cost greatly hinder their utility. Dark enemies are notorious for their insanely high DPS which can and will tear through this unit in a matter of seconds, in spite of their high effective health (178,500 at Lv.30, and 283,500 at Lv.50, assuming all [[Void Fruit]] Treasures are maxed). Without a stream of expensive replacements to fill any gaps in the frontline, they cannot hope to stop said threats on its own, let alone in mixed stages where Darks are supported by other nasty enemies, although they could be of use against Darks with longer attack cycles like [[Director Kurosawah]], [[Le'noir]], or [[Two Can]].

Yellow Nyanko Ranger does possess a unique "Wave Immunity" Effect [[Cat Combo|Combo]] that can give themselves and other [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] a niche against [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|enemy Wave Attackers]]. Additionally, they can be used to great effect with [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] to decrease this unit's recharge rate and cost respectively. The sheer power of these Nyanko Rangers and their Cat Combos/synergies prevents this Cat from being terrible outright, but it only lightly addresses the main problems on top of requiring additional slots.

They continue to struggle later in the game due to rapidly escalating enemy strength magnifications on top of existing competition, with the likes of [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]], [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Frolicking Nono CC]] and [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]] possessing superior specialist performance. For all of the aforementioned reasons, this cat usually only ever sees a home in the [[Underground Labyrinth]].

